      "rests_on": [],
      "reasoning": "In the debate Hilton said 'we need to incentivize jobs to be created in California', which leans away from 'Don't give companies tax breaks or subsidies' but names no conditions, wage or local-hire terms, clawback, or cost limits. His campaign pages (an uncapped film incentive that rewards hiring California workers; pharmaceutical enterprise zones tied to production and jobs) are third-person plan text and mix elements of several rungs, so none of 'only if they commit to good wages and local hiring', 'keep limits and pass on deals that cost too much', or 'no conditions or spending limits' is established.",
      "needs_source": [],
      "quotes": [
        {
          "snapshot_id": "171a62e8-4acd-55b9-892f-dc22954f54be",
          "text": "So we need to incentivize jobs to be created in California instead of sending them to Texas.",
          "v7_tier": "direction",
          "v7_flag": null,
          "v8_quotable": true,
          "v8_codes": []
        },
        {
          "snapshot_id": "bf9e7ef4-4c83-53b8-8d47-b8e9737ddd28",
          "text": "Move to an uncapped, open production incentive system",
          "v7_tier": "lever",
          "v7_flag": "lever-named",
          "v8_quotable": true,
          "v8_codes": []
        },
        {
          "snapshot_id": "74a0d89d-9d6c-5a91-baca-797d374524ca",
          "text": "Pharmaceutical enterprise zones in the Central Valley and Inland Empire will offer tax and regulatory relief to companies that actually manufacture essential and generic medicines here. No production and no California jobs means no incentive.",
          "v7_tier": "lever",
          "v7_flag": "lever-named",
          "v8_quotable": true,
          "v8_codes": []
        },
        {
          "snapshot_id": "fa380fe6-1e05-5d5a-aa81-349e62796fe5",
          "text": "California’s policy regime should be unequivocally on the side of job- and wealth-creators.",
          "v7_tier": "direction",
